@weirdan the only practical example I can foresee is phpunit, but `TestCase::expectException()` implies `@psalm-suppress MissingThrowsDocblock T` if it were stubbed out in psalm/phpunit-psalm-plugin as:

```php
/**
* @template T as Throwable
*
* @param class-string<T> $throwable
*/
public function expectException(string $throwable) { }
```

i.e.
```php
public function testThing() : void {
  static::expectException(RuntimeException::class)
  
  throw new RuntimeException('foo');
}
```
